proposals.beats:
TopTierPrep's vocabulary and question bank never meet. Their Words in Context pool is fixed (261 College Board + 102 of their own), their own Transitions pool is 10 items, and nothing brings a missed item back later. Ours:
- every word item is a real SAT-format item that never runs out;
- every miss comes back fresh on a schedule until it holds;
- R&W gets Review, check-ins and Up next the day Words ships.
This is also the additive first step of decision 3: the first EBRW bank templates.

parity_gaps.spec_says:
The main 'what they missed' items:
- In a real question;
- Practice 10 questions with it;
- math mix-up Drill it;
- Mistake → words;
- tap-to-define in math stems;
- Translate the phrase;
- the Math word of the day;
- Looked up from math stems.

parity_gaps.upgrade:
Replace the Math-bank link with an R&W one:
- R&W items as bank templates with traps and check-ins (P2);
- named traps on every wrong option (P1);
- word gap vs reading gap diagnosis (P8).
Feed 'Looked up' from Commit-first misses and placement 'No' answers instead of math stems. Swap the Math word of the day for a transition logic of the day or a root of the day.

A star means 'I want this for test day':
- the word jumps the New queue;
- it counts in the finish line (P9);
- if not reviewed in 14 days, it comes back in Today's words;
- it gets the exam cap even at box 5.

Show outcomes on Me:
